Most of the techniques had such a large cooldown, that I didn't use
them, because I felt like I needed to save them "just in case"
something really bad happened.  The biggest exception was Tinker,
which basically made Gnomish Healers completely ridiculous.  The basic
idea is that you would Tinker, Tinker, Tinker your inventory, while
eating meat boulders to give you enough nutrition to repeatedly Tinker
stuff.  Tinker gives you access to the upgrade chart (http://
www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/slashem/potions.html), which allows you to
do things like turning a "Dwarvish cloak" into a "Cloak of Magic
Resistance".  Yes, you would be spending a really large number of
turns to Tinker all your equipment, but it didn't take very much real-
time to get a big chunk of an ascension kit by Tinkering the junk that
is found in the Gnomish Mines.


